                            **USER management**

**Types of users in linux:
1. Root user:
--> root user is a super user in system, who has all access pass to the system functionality.

2. Standard user:
--> standrd users are those users which are created by root user. 
-they have limited permissions compared to the root user.

3. system user:
--> system users are the users account created by the system rather than root user
who used to run background processes and services

docker
mysql



adduser/useradd  <user_name>
--> this command is used to create standard user
eg: adduser amit

/etc/passwd : display user information
/etc/shadow : display user password information

seema  :  x  :  1001  :  1001  :   :  /home/seema  : /bin/bash
  1       2       3       4      5         6            7

1 : user name
2 : password
3 : user ID
4 : group ID
5 : user other information
6 : user home directory
7 : shell type


usermod -u <new-uid> <user-name>
--> to change user's uid
usermod -u 7001 seema

usermod -g <new-gid> <user_name>
--> to change user's gid
usermod -g 1001 seema

usermod -c "comments" <user_name>
--> to update user information
usermod -c "seema patil, Pune, 0123456789" seema

usermod -d <new-home-dir> <user_name>
--> to change user's home directory
usermod -d /mnt seema

usermod -s <new-shell_type> <user_name>
--> to chnage shell type
usermod -s /bin/sh seema

usermod -l <new_name> <old_user_name>
--> to rename user
usermod -l seema seeema

usermod -L <user_name>
-> to lock user account
usemod -L seema

usermod -U <user_name>
--> to unlock user account
usermod -U seema

passwd <user_name>
--> used to change password of user
eg: passwd seema

reserved UID's:
0 = root
1 - 999 = system users
1000+ = standard users

userdel <user_name>
--> to delete user from system
userdel seema


                             **group management**

groupadd <group_name>
--> to create group
groupadd aws

groupdel <group_name>
--> to delete group
groupdel aws

/etc/group : to display group information
 
 aws  :  x  :  5003  :
  1      2      3       4

  1 : group name
  2 : group password
  3 : group id
  4 : group members

  group types:
  1. primary group
  2. secondary group

  usermod -aG <group_name> <user_name>
  --> to add single user to the group
  usermod -aG aws  seema

  gpasswd -M <user1>,<user2>,<user3>... <group_name>
  --> to add multiple users into group
  gpasswd -M seema,mena,atul aws

  gpasswd -d <user_name> <group_name>
  --> to delete user from group
  gpasswd -d seema aws

  groupmod -n <new_group_name> <old_group_name>
  --> to rename group
  groupmod -n devops aws
 

 






